{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21fb7e39d99b57bc5bb1", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Practical Chemistry - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913117"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130d2", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891306b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4724"], "question": {"text": "In the flame test of a mixture of salts, a green flame with blue centre was observed. Which one of the following cations may be present?"}, "options": [{"id": "8c9fcb", "text": "Calcium", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891306c"}, {"id": "acc904", "text": "Copper", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891306d"}, {"id": "bbfaf4", "text": "Barium", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891306e"}, {"id": "333dd5", "text": "Strontium", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891306f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913070", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["6162fc136ed13040ec85660f"], "question": {"text": "Formation of which complex, among the following, is not a confirmatory test of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions"}, "options": [{"id": "1079d4", "text": "Lead sulphate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913071"}, {"id": "258bb6", "text": "Lead nitrate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913072"}, {"id": "ac3cad", "text": "Lead chromate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913073"}, {"id": "c19b2f", "text": "Lead iodide", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913074"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913075", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4790"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f33"], "question": {"text": "Formation of $\\mathrm{Na}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_5 \\mathrm{NOS}\\right]$, a purple coloured complex formed by addition of sodium nitroprusside in sodium carbonate extract of salt indicates the presence of :"}, "options": [{"id": "ff76e1", "text": "Sodium ion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913076"}, {"id": "edfdf5", "text": "Sulphate ion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913077"}, {"id": "71fa53", "text": "Sulphide ion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913078"}, {"id": "6bfb67", "text": "Sulphite ion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913079"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891307a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ef7"], "question": {"text": "The compound that is white in color is"}, "options": [{"id": "40a70f", "text": "ammonium sulphide", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891307b"}, {"id": "44808d", "text": "lead sulphate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891307c"}, {"id": "920621", "text": "lead iodide", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891307d"}, {"id": "1c87ee", "text": "ammonium arsinomolybdate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891307e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891307f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5661"], "question": {"text": "Match List - I with List - II :<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List - I&nbsp;(Metal ion)</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List - II (Group in Qualitative analysis)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(a)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(i)</td>\t\t\t<td>Group - III</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(b)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>As</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(ii)</td>\t\t\t<td>Group - IIA</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(c)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iii)</td>\t\t\t<td>Group -&nbsp;IV</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(d)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iv)</td>\t\t\t<td>Group - IIB</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "074685", "text": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913080"}, {"id": "dc6408", "text": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913081"}, {"id": "609560", "text": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913082"}, {"id": "dc10f2", "text": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913083"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913084", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4790"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4749"], "question": {"text": "Choose the correct tests with respective observations.<br />(A) \\(\\mathrm{CuSO}_4\\) (acidified with acetic acid) \\(+ \\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right] \\rightarrow\\) Chocolate brown precipitate.<br />(B) \\(\\mathrm{FeCl}_3+\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right] \\rightarrow\\) Prussian blue precipitate.<br />(C) \\(\\mathrm{ZnCl}_2+\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]\\), neutralised with \\(\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH}\\) \\(\\rightarrow\\) White or bluish white precipitate.<br />(D) \\(\\mathrm{MgCl}_2+\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right] \\rightarrow\\) Blue precipitate.<br />(E) \\(\\mathrm{BaCl}_2+\\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]\\), neutralised with NaOH \\(\\rightarrow\\) White precipitate.<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "c2d900", "text": "A, D and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913085"}, {"id": "4962c5", "text": "B, D and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913086"}, {"id": "a56532", "text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913087"}, {"id": "5bb748", "text": "C, D and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913088"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913089", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["617aaa13ef3fe65ad8e85de5"], "question": {"text": "An organic compound &lsquo;A&rsquo; is oxidized with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> followed by boiling with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The resultant solution is then treated with ammonium molybdate to yield a yellow percipitate. Based on a above observation, the element present in the given compound is:"}, "options": [{"id": "04939e", "text": "Fluorine", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891308a"}, {"id": "056a68", "text": "Phosphorus", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891308b"}, {"id": "753c2e", "text": "Nitrogen", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891308c"}, {"id": "bff4b0", "text": "Sulphur", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891308d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891308e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["6162fc136ed13040ec85660b"], "question": {"text": "Match List I with List II\n\\(\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|}\n\\hline & \\text{List - I} & & \\text{List - II} \\\\\n& \\text{(Precipitating reagent and conditions)} & & \\text{(Cation)} \\\\\n\\hline \\text { A. } & \\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH} / \\mathrm{ARKS} & \\text { I. } & \\mathrm{Mn}^{2+} \\\\\n\\hline \\text { B. } & \\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3 & \\text { II. } & \\mathrm{Pb}^{2+} \\\\\n\\hline \\text { C. } & \\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{~S} \\text { gas } & \\text { III. } & \\mathrm{Al}^{3+} \\\\\n\\hline \\text { D. } & \\text { dilute } \\mathrm{HCl} & \\text { IV. } & \\mathrm{Sr}^{2+} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\\)\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "6b138a", "text": "A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891308f"}, {"id": "0269ff", "text": "A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913090"}, {"id": "749f49", "text": "A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913091"}, {"id": "dbc8cb", "text": "A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913092"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913093", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4790"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4749"], "question": {"text": "When a salt is treated with sodium hydroxide solution it gives gas $\\mathrm{X}$. On passing gas $\\mathrm{X}$ through reagent $\\mathrm{Y}$ a brown coloured precipitate is formed. $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ respectively, are"}, "options": [{"id": "14c307", "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{NH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{HgO}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913094"}, {"id": "799db8", "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{NH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{HgI}_4+\\mathrm{KOH}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913095"}, {"id": "3db795", "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{KOH}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913096"}, {"id": "8e5397", "text": "$\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913097"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913098", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["617aaa13ef3fe65ad8e85df5"], "question": {"text": "During the borax bead test with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, a blue green colour of the bead was observed in oxidising flame due to the formation of"}, "options": [{"id": "792bc9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913099"}, {"id": "60a970", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891309a"}, {"id": "fc2c39", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891309b"}, {"id": "3c6a2e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuO</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891309c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891309d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["64889bba8be547b3b654fae2"], "question": {"text": "In the wet tests for detection of various cations by precipitation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> cations are detected by obtaining precipitate of"}, "options": [{"id": "1904fc", "text": "Ba(ox) : Barium oxalate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891309e"}, {"id": "c8ae88", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a891309f"}, {"id": "607057", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ba</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OAc</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a0"}, {"id": "40f263", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e5a"], "question": {"text": "<p>Which statement is not true with respect to nitrate ion test?</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e8eadc", "text": "A dark brown ring is formed at the junction of two solutions.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a3"}, {"id": "e3c32e", "text": "Ring is formed due to nitroferrous sulphate complex.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a4"}, {"id": "58449c", "text": "The brown complex is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>NO</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a5"}, {"id": "add31e", "text": "Heating the nitrate salt with conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, light brown fumes are evolved.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bf"], "question": {"text": "In the wet tests for identification of various cations by precipitation, which transition element cation doesn&#39;t belong to group IV in qualitative inorganic analysis?"}, "options": [{"id": "32efeb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a8"}, {"id": "28e47a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130a9"}, {"id": "22c885", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130aa"}, {"id": "2f2976", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130ab"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130ac", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["6162fc136ed13040ec85661c"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List-I with List-II&nbsp;</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">List-I</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">List-II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Test/Reagents/Observation(s)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Species detected</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(a)</td>\t\t\t<td>Lassaigne&#39;s Test</td>\t\t\t<td>(i)</td>\t\t\t<td>Carbon</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(b)</td>\t\t\t<td>Cu(II) oxide</td>\t\t\t<td>(ii)</td>\t\t\t<td>Sulphur</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(c)</td>\t\t\t<td>Silver nitrate</td>\t\t\t<td>(iii)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>, and halogen</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(d)</td>\t\t\t<td>The sodium fusion extract gives black precipitate with acetic acid and lead acet