f an inorganic salt. Further,&nbsp;a gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;with characteristic odour was released&nbsp;when the formed white precipitate was dissolved in&nbsp;dilute HCI. The anion present in the inorganic salt is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f6f2cf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130b7"}, {"id": "b95724", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130b8"}, {"id": "df6e89", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130b9"}, {"id": "c71f2d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130ba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130bb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5661"], "question": {"text": "To an aqueous solution containing ions such as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;was&nbsp;added <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>conc</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>, followed by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>. The total number of cations precipitated during this reaction is/are :"}, "options": [{"id": "402d05", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130bc"}, {"id": "2d754f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130bd"}, {"id": "0b73a3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130be"}, {"id": "895fc0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130bf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4724"], "question": {"text": "Match List - I with List - II.\n\\(\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\text{List - I} & \\text{List - II} \\\\\n\\text{Reaction} & \\text{Type of redox reaction} \\\\\n\\text{(A) } \\mathrm{Li} & \\text{(I) } 589.2 \\\\\n\\text{(B) } \\mathrm{Na} & \\text{(II) } 455.5 \\\\\n\\text{(C) } \\mathrm{Rb} & \\text{(III) } 670.8 \\\\\n\\text{(D) } \\mathrm{Cs} & \\text{(IV) } 780.0 \\\\\n\\end{array}\\)\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "d8e09b", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c1"}, {"id": "eb7988", "text": "(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c2"}, {"id": "e41fa4", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c3"}, {"id": "90e62f", "text": "(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52eb"], "concepts": ["6162fc136ed13040ec85660f"], "question": {"text": "Identify $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}$ and C in the given below reaction sequence\n$\\mathrm{A} \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{HNO}_3} \\mathrm{~Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_3\\right)_2 \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4}$ B $\\xrightarrow[\\substack{\\text { (2) Acetic acid } \\\\ \\text { (3) } \\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{CrO}_4}]{\\substack{\\text { (1) Ammonium } \\\\ \\text { acetate }}}$"}, "options": [{"id": "88c2c8", "text": "$\\mathrm{PbCl}_2, \\mathrm{PbSO}_4, \\mathrm{PbCrO}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c6"}, {"id": "1fb63a", "text": "$\\mathrm{PbS}, \\mathrm{PbSO}_4, \\mathrm{~Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{COO}\\right)_2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c7"}, {"id": "12bd42", "text": "$\\mathrm{PbCl}_2, \\mathrm{~Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{SO}_4\\right)_2, \\mathrm{PbCrO}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c8"}, {"id": "a36ce8", "text": "$\\mathrm{PbS}, \\mathrm{PbSO}_4, \\mathrm{PbCrO}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130c9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130ca", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205af"], "topics": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9cd"], "concepts": ["617aaa13ef3fe65ad8e85df5"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:<br />Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;Colourless cupric metaborate is reduced to cuprous metaborate in a luminous flame.</p><p>Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Cuprous metaborate is obtained by heating boric anhydride and copper sulphate in a non-luminous flame.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "52ecbd", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130cb"}, {"id": "276bde", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130cc"}, {"id": "96f35e", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130cd"}, {"id": "99ea91", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a89130ce"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:15.618Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:15.618Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913115"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f3bc677dc36a8913113", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de